James inquired about a Python function definition that produced a `TypeError` due to the use of a union type hint syntax (`px: pd.Series | None`), which is not supported in Python versions prior to 3.10. I explained that the error arises from this syntax and provided a solution by suggesting the use of `Union` from the `typing` module for compatibility with earlier versions. I offered a revised code snippet using `Union[pd.Series, None]` and indicated that upgrading to Python 3.10 or later would allow the use of the shorthand type hinting.
